    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "35145de2_38bad5a5",
        "filename": "src/dawn/native/d3d12/PlatformFunctionsD3D12.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 19
      },
      "lineNbr": 106,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000262
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-05-12T00:35:25Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Since you\u0027ve enabled the Dawn Toggle by default, we should simplify the code her by creating the device factory unconditionally. The Dawn toggle should determine whether we use the factory to create the device (toggle \u003d\u003d true) or just `D3D12CreateDevice` (toggle \u003d\u003d false). Calling `D3D12CreateDevice` after creating the factory will result in a device which doesn\u0027t use the AgilitySDK.\n\nThis way, we don\u0027t have to obsess about InitAgilitySDK called at the right time. Instead, it always runs.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 106,
        "startChar": 16,
        "endLine": 106,
        "endChar": 35
      },
      "revId": "7278830c260c7916aabed12d754fe7cc8b5cc304",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "e7457193_b5526576",
        "filename": "src/dawn/native/d3d12/PlatformFunctionsD3D12.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 19
      },
      "lineNbr": 106,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000262
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-05-12T00:35:25Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "After creating the factory, please call `SetFlags` and pass `D3D12_DEVICE_FACTORY_FLAG_ALLOW_RETURNING_EXISTING_DEVICE`.  This way, we can share the D3D12 device with the Chromium media engine when the device configurations are compatible. Otherwise, two instances of the UMD will be created in the process, chewing through memory unnecessarily.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 106,
        "startChar": 16,
        "endLine": 106,
        "endChar": 36
      },
      "revId": "7278830c260c7916aabed12d754fe7cc8b5cc304",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
